===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰuH-}}
From {{der|en|af|Boer||Boer}}, from {{m|af|boer||farmer}}. {{doublet|en|bauer|boor|bower|id3=farmer}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} A Dutch [[colonist]] in [[South Africa]] during the colonial era, especially a [[farmer]].
#: {{hypo|en|trekboer}}
# A [[militant]] in the {{w|Boer War}}.
#: {{ux|en|The British soldiers captured a '''Boer''' after the battle.}}
# {{lb|en|derogatory|offensive}} An [[Afrikaner]], especially a [[farmer]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1979|author=w:André Brink|title=A Dry White Season|page=93|publisher=Vintage|year_published=1998
|passage=‘I won't say good day to a fucking '''''boer'''''!’ he exploded, swinging round viciously to escape into the angry light outside.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Erica L. Green|title=Trump Lectures South African President in Televised Oval Office Confrontation|work=The New York Times|date=2025-05-21|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/21/us/politics/trump-ramaphosa-south-africa-visit.html|issn=0362-4331|author2=Zolan Kanno-Youngs|passage=At least one of the scenes on the screen appeared to be the rallying cry of “Kill the '''Boer''',” which U.S. officials and Afrikaner activists have cited as evidence that white South Africans are being persecuted. Boer means farmer in Dutch and Afrikaans.}}

